From 50d968ae6e05e9b898e21928783ac3c1ea6fe287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:51:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 102/118] decode-link: Shadowsocks, SOCKS, Hysteria 2, TUIC,
 VMess, HTTP, Hysteria, AnyTLS and NaiveProxy links

Each in the forms its generators write:

- ss: SIP002 with the user in base64 or, for the methods of 2022, as it is; the older
  form with everything in base64; plugin (simple-obfs is obfs-local), uot;
- socks5, socks5h, socks4, socks4a, and the socks:// of v2rayN with the user in base64;
- hysteria2 and hy2: a list of ports in the place of the port or in mport, obfs, the
  speeds;
- tuic: uuid:password, the congestion control, the relay mode, zero RTT, heartbeat;
- vmess: the JSON in base64 of v2rayN and the URL form, with the transports and the TLS
  of the VLESS links;
- http and https as a proxy, only with a port and without a path: anything else is the
  address of a page or of a subscription;
- hysteria (the first one), anytls, naive+https and naive+quic.

Refused, each under its rule in the table: Shadowsocks over a transport or TLS of
Xray, TUIC v4, the faketcp and wechat-video modes of Hysteria.

The version line gets one name, tls.utls-fallback: the uTLS fingerprint fallback, which
a script may want to switch. What the build decodes is not announced there: a link of a
type the build was made without is refused with the words of the build ("vmess outbound
is not included in this build ..., install podkop-engine-full ...").
